  "explains": "server.servlet.context-path in application.properties moves from /ledger to /billing. The context path is put before every route of the application, so every route the table has at the head is reached: thirteen routes of InvoiceController (seven), StatusController (two), AuditController, CustomerController (two, the Kotlin one) and ReportController, all under /billing; the first line of each chain is the changed line, and the last line of the evidence of each route is the context path. The old routes under /ledger are gone. The web client still calls four of them (fetchInvoices, fetchInvoice, fetchTotal and fetchStatus): four removed routes still called, each a finding with high risk and low confidence, four http edges to routes that are removed, and after the change none of the four URLs fits a route, so the edge says so (four client_url_unmatched and a blocking edge_incomplete). The client calls are followed to the screens /invoices, /invoices/:invoiceId and /status.",
